s", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 110, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[124, 124]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 111, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[125, 125]], "note": "'Confidence Intervals' subheading"}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[126, 126]], "assertion": "primary estimand (risk difference) confidence interval was obtained via parametric bootstrap with 1,000 iterations", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["confidence interval", "bootstrap"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[127, 127]], "assertion": "bootstrap coefficient vectors were randomly sampled from a multivariate normal distribution defined by the estimated parameters and variance-covariance matrix", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 114, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[128, 128]], "assertion": "risk difference was calculated for each bootstrap sample", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["bootstrap", "risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[129, 129]], "assertion": "95% CI was taken from the 2.5th and 97.5th percentiles of the bootstrap distribution", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["confidence interval"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 116, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[130, 130]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 117, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[131, 131]], "assertion": "secondary estimand (odds ratio) confidence interval was obtained via profile likelihood from the logistic regression model", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["confidence interval", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 118, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[132, 132]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 119, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[133, 133]], "note": "'P-values' label"}, {"id": 120, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[134, 134]], "assertion": "risk-difference p-value was computed as a two-sided test based on the proportion of bootstrap samples on each side of zero", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["p-value", "bootstrap"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 121, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[135, 135]], "assertion": "odds-ratio p-value was computed via a Wald test using cluster-robust standard errors", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["p-value", "odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[136, 136]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[137, 137]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[138, 138]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 125, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[139, 139]], "note": "'Conclusion' section heading"}, {"id": 126, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[140, 140]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[141, 141]], "assertion": "overall conclusion headline: NOT SUPPORTED", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[142, 142]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[143, 143]], "assertion": "the hypothesis that referees are more likely to give red cards to dark-skinned than light-skinned players is not supported by this analysis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["hypothesis", "skin tone", "red cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 130, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[144, 144]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[145, 145]], "note": "'Rationale' subheading"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[146, 146]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[147, 147]], "assertion": "the adjusted risk difference of 0.17 percentage points is characterized as a small effect size; text is garbled/truncated but suggests a caveat that the games measure may not fully capture exposure to red-card opportunities", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference", "effect size", "number of games"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[148, 148]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[149, 149]], "note": "'Potential Unmeasured Confounding' subheading"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[150, 150]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 137, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[151, 151]], "note": "caveat that the observational design only allows controlling for measured confounders"}, {"id": 138, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[152, 152]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 139, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[153, 153]], "note": "caveat that player behavior/playing style is a potential unmeasured confounder"}, {"id": 140, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[154, 154]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[155, 155]], "note": "caveat that player reputation is a potential unmeasured confounder"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[156, 156]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 143, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[157, 157]], "note": "caveat that team tactics/strategy is a potential unmeasured confounder"}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[158, 158]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "referee fixed effects and referee-level covariates were not included in the model", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee fixed effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [146]}, {"id": 146, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[159, 159]], "assertion": "country-level implicit bias measures were excluded from the main model", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["implicit bias measures"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [145]}, {"id": 147, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[160, 160]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[161, 161]], "note": "caveat that match context data (importance, score differential, crowd behavior) is lacking"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[162, 162]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[163, 163]], "note": "'Assumptions and Model Specification' subheading"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[164, 164]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 152, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 165]], "assertion": "assumed linear effects of continuous covariates (games, height, weight) on log-odds", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [153]}, {"id": 153, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[165, 165]], "assertion": "did not explore non-linearities or interactions among continuous covariates", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["model specification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [152]}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[166, 166]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[167, 167]], "assertion": "did not test for interactions between skin tone and other variables (position, league, referee country)", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["interactions", "effect modification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "visual inspection suggested adequate overlap between dark- and light-skinned players across covariate combinations", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["positivity assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [158]}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "formal positivity checks were not conducted", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["positivity assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [157]}, {"id": 159, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "assumed the logistic regression model is correctly specified", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["model specification"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 161, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[172, 172]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 162, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "did not account for potential clustering by referee or by match in standard errors", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["standard errors", "clustering"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [163]}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[173, 173]], "assertion": "the potential underestimation of standard errors from unaccounted referee/match clustering would not change the substantive conclusion, since results are already non-significant", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard errors", "conclusion"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [162]}, {"id": 164, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "with only 1.26% of dyads having red cards, rare-events bias is a concern but is mitigated by the large sample size (N=115,603)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["rare events", "sample size"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[176, 176]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[177, 177]], "note": "'Generalizability and External Validity' subheading"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[178, 178]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "caveat that results may not generalize beyond the four leagues and 2012-2013 season studied"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[180, 180]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "caveat that soccer has changed since 2012-2013 (e.g. VAR, referee-bias attention), so current environment may differ"}, {"id": 172, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[182, 182]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[183, 183]], "note": "caveat that results, from elite professional soccer, may not generalize to amateur/youth/lower-division leagues"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[184, 184]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[185, 185]], "note": "caveat that cultural context of skin tone varies and country-level implicit bias measures may not capture individual referee bias or within-country variation"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 177, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[187, 187]], "note": "'Sensitivity and Robustness' subheading"}, {"id": 178, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[188, 188]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 179, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "sensitivity analyses that could have strengthened the conclusions were not conducted", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 180, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[190, 190]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "0.5 was used as the cutpoint for dark/light skin classification", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone cutpoint"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [182]}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[191, 191]], "assertion": "alternative cutpoints (e.g. tertiles, quartiles) or a continuous specification were not used but might have produced different results", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["skin tone cutpoint"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [181]}, {"id": 183, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 184, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "multiple imputation for missing data, to assess robustness to missingness assumptions, was not conducted", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["missing data", "imputation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[194, 194]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[195, 195]], "assertion": "referee fixed effects or multilevel models, to better account for referee-level clustering and heterogeneity, were not used", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["referee fixed effects", "multilevel models"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[197, 197]], "assertion": "interaction analyses to test effect modification by league, position, referee country, or implicit bias were not conducted", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["interactions"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[198, 198]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[199, 199]], "assertion": "propensity score methods, as an alternative to regression adjustment, were not used to assess robustness", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["propensity score methods"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[200, 200]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[201, 201]], "assertion": "alternative outcome definitions (e.g. count models, specific red-card types) were not analyzed", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["outcome variable", "red cards"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 193, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[202, 202]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 194, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "'Summary of Limitations' subheading"}, {"id": 195, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[204, 204]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 196, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[205, 205]], "note": "transition sentence introducing the limitations list, self-characterizing the analysis as rigorous"}, {"id": 197, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[206, 206]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[207, 207]], "note": "general caveat that observational data limit causal inference due to potential unmeasured confounding"}, {"id": 199, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[208, 208]], "assertion": "missing data comprised about 21% of the original sample, which could introduce selection bias", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["missing data", "sample size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 200, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[209, 209]], "note": "caveat that measurement error in skin tone (subjective photo ratings) could attenuate or bias estimates"}, {"id": 201, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[210, 210]], "note": "caveat that the rare outcome leads to wide confidence intervals and limited statistical power"}, {"id": 202, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[211, 211]], "note": "caveat that model assumptions (linearity, no interactions, correct specification) may not fully hold"}, {"id": 203, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[212, 212]], "note": "caveat that generalizability is limited to the leagues, season, and context studied"}, {"id": 204, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 205, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "the analysis is characterized as having employed appropriate, transparent, and reproducible statistical methods, adjusting for important confounders", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["methodology"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [206, 207]}, {"id": 206, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "the conclusion that the hypothesis is not supported is asserted to be justified given the data and methods used", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [205, 207]}, {"id": 207, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[214, 214]], "assertion": "additional research with refined methods or larger samples is suggested as valuable but was not conducted here", "polarity": "would_have", "targets": ["future research"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [205, 206]}, {"id": 208, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[215, 215]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 209, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[216, 216]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 210, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[217, 217]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 211, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[218, 218]], "note": "'Reproducibility Statement' heading"}, {"id": 212, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[219, 219]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 213, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[220, 220]], "assertion": "all analyses were conducted in Python using publicly available data, with full analysis code provided in final_analysis.py", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility", "code"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 214, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[221, 221]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 215, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[222, 228]], "assertion": "the analysis code includes data loading/preparation, descriptive statistics, logistic regression with cluster-robust SEs, g-computation for risk difference, parametric bootstrap CIs (1,000 iterations, seed=42), odds-ratio calculation with CIs, and result visualization", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility", "code"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 216, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[229, 229]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 217, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[230, 230]], "assertion": "results can be fully reproduced by running the provided code with the original dataset (./data/soccer/soccer.csv)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reproducibility"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 218, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[231, 231]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 219, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[232, 232]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 220, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[233, 233]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 221, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[234, 234]], "note": "'References' heading"}, {"id": 222, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[235, 235]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 223, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[236, 236]], "note": "dataset provenance: 2,053 players and 3,147 referees across the four leagues (2012-13 season), skin tone coded by two raters from photos, dyad-level encounter/card data"}, {"id": 224, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[237, 237]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 225, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[238, 238]], "note": "'Statistical Methods' label"}, {"id": 226, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "citation", "lines": [[239, 239]], "note": "Hosmer, Lemeshow & Sturdivant (2013) citation"}, {"id": 227, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "citation", "lines": [[240, 240]], "note": "Snowden, Rose & Mortimer (2011) citation"}, {"id": 228, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "citation", "lines": [[241, 241]], "note": "Cameron & Miller (2015) citation"}, {"id": 229, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[242, 242]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 230, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[243, 243]], "note": "horizontal rule divider"}, {"id": 231, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[244, 244]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 232, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[245, 245]], "note": "'End of Report' label"}, {"id": 233, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[246, 246]], "note": "blank line"}, {"id": 234, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[247, 247]], "note": "tool-output closing wrapper tag"}]}}